* WHL - WHEEL PRIVILEGE CONTROL

SYSOP ONLY. Private utility; use the local sysop console.

A - Purpose, syntax and examples

:A
* WHL - WHEEL PRIVILEGE CONTROL

SYSOP ONLY. Private utility; use the local sysop console.

Syntax:
    WHL

Controls the Z-System wheel privilege flag. The installed command itself
is wheel-protected. It is not a public privilege request or caller login
command.

Use the established private sysop workflow and AUTH policy controls. Never
publish privilege credentials, enable wheel for callers, or treat a help
page as execution permission.

See HELP COMMANDS for the command index.
